    "narrative": "The Austin Waves roster presents a balanced attack today, though **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (72.18) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.01) lead the charge as our most viable cornerstones. Both benefit from favorable matchups against mid-rotation arms; **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** leverages an elite 15% SP skill advantage against Dobnak, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** capitalizes on a strong 14% dynamic platoon edge against King. **Sam Antonacci** and **Miguel Vargas** also offer high-floor value (63.14 and 62.46, respectively) by attacking Ober. With Ober\u2019s 4.79 xERA and a generous 92% steal-success probability threshold, **Miguel Vargas** is an opportunistic start, as his speed metrics are specifically optimized for this matchup.\n\nStrategic discipline remains key given our focus on the scarcest category: Stolen Bases. While **Kyle Tucker** (66.85) remains a must-start, we are monitoring the lineup for **Nasim Nunez**; should he slot into the #9 hole as projected, his 85% steal-success rate against the slow delivery of Wrobleski keeps him in the starting XI despite the order penalty. The most difficult bench decision involved **Coby Mayo** (56.06); while his platoon edge against Tolle is significant, the 50% \"Elite Hold\" rate of the opposing pitcher makes it a high-risk environment for aggressive base-running. Consequently, we are sacrificing his power potential to prioritize the more consistent production profiles of our top OFs.\n\nCaution is warranted for **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jackson Merrill**, both of whom face high-caliber pitching in Tolle and Cole. While **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from park factors, the 13% SP skill drag significantly dampens his ceiling. Meanwhile, **Wade Meckler** (40.30) sits right on our efficiency floor; despite the platoon advantage, the matchup against Skenes\u2014who represents the ultimate threat to our daily production targets\u2014makes this a volatile start. We continue to hold **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson** on the IL, alongside depth pieces like **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Tommy White**, **Curtis Mead**, **Franklin Arias**, **Dominic Smith**, **Liam Hicks**, and **Luis Lara**, waiting for clearer runway in the final stretch of the season.",
